#!/bin/bash
# hypr-rdp's on_session_start/end hooks never fire (IronRDP takes the
# connection handler out during a session). Derive session start/end from
# hypr-rdp's own log lines instead and run hypr-rdp-session accordingly.
journalctl --user -u hypr-rdp -f -n 0 -o cat | while IFS= read -r line; do
  case "$line" in
    *"Clipboard channel ready"*)         hypr-rdp-session start ;;  # every connect, any codec
    *"Display update channel closed"*)   hypr-rdp-session end ;;
  esac
done
